## PRIORITY 1 — EI/RS calculation-integrity (math must be right first)

### T1. EI assessment-methodology + non-detect handling (the "systematically low" bug)
EI forces every qualitative `<X% of permitted` / `meets Option 1` / `% of permitted` declaration to concentration 0 in `annexure_converter.resolve_element_reading` (status `below_option1_qualitative`) and again in `ei_core._EI_ZERO_STATUSES` / `_ei_element_reads_zero` / `resolve_element_calculation_value` (`policy in ("non_detect_zero","excluded_by_declaration") → 0.0`). This reproduces only Vasopressin (qualitative→0, an explicitly documented report policy) and contradicts Esomeprazole (Dextrose = 0.30×permitted: Pb 0.15/As 0.45/V 3/Ni 6), Diazoxide (detection/spec/max-expected) and Medroxy (declared vendor concentrations). Remove the A3 comment mis-citing Esomeprazole as authority for the zero convention it contradicts.
- Add `ei_assessment_method` to the request scope via the **existing** mechanism (mirror `rs_framework` exactly: same plumbing `docgen_api.generate_report` → request scope → `_build_ei` → `calculate_ei_tables`). Values: `conservative_bound` (**DEFAULT**) and `qualitative_zero`. No new config surface beyond this one flag.
- **Critical correction (this is why "nothing changed"):** under `conservative_bound`, an element carrying a bound — an explicit printed `<X` reporting limit / LOD / LOQ (captured by the less-than regex), a page floor like `(LOQ-0.05)`, or an `mrl` value — must contribute **that bound, NOT zero**. Change `less_than / bdl / blq / below_detection / derived_loq / not_tested` so they resolve to `source_bound` under `conservative_bound` and to `0.0` under `qualitative_zero`. A genuine ND with **no** printed bound stays 0 under both. The prior spec line "ND/BDL/BLQ/<LOD always 0 under both" was wrong — it is the sole reason ~10 Esomeprazole excipients render all-zero (Sugar Spheres BLQ/(LOQ-0.05), Polysorbate `<0.05/<0.20/<0.50`, Kollidon `<0.05`, Citric Acid `<0.06/<0.10/<0.15`, Klucel "Not Detected" LOD 0.06/LOQ 0.2) against the approved conservative bounds.
- The `<30% of permitted` branch → `conservative_bound` = 0.30×Option-1 permitted; `qualitative_zero` = 0 (Dextrose). Governed by the same flag.
- Default with nothing configured = `conservative_bound`.

### T2. EI measurement-dropping in the two-column CoA layout (higher-impact than T1)
Real measured values above the reporting limit are being read as non-detects and zeroed. The "Content measured or range" + "Report Limit (RL)" two-column layout (Peter Greven Mag Stearate V ~2030 ppb, Ni ~1340 ppb, Ba ~1790 ppb — tilde `~/∼` prefix) and Ashland "Highest value from lots tested = 0.7 ppm" print **measurements**, not `<RL`. In `annexure_converter`: when the Content column holds a number (optionally prefixed `~ / ∼ / approx`), it is the result (`status=actual`, normalize ppb→µg/g); only fall back to the RL column when Content is `<RL` / blank. Ensure the presence-flagged-bound path also fires on "Potentially present = Yes/X". Expected: Mag Stearate V=2.03, Ni=1.34 µg/g; Klucel Ni=0.7; and with T1, Pb total reconciles toward approved 3.207 (not 2.67).

### T3. EI layered-evidence preservation
Stop collapsing qualitative/limit cells to a bare 0. `resolve_element_reading` / `process_annexure` emit per element: `source_state`, `source_numeric_value` (nullable), `source_bound`, `calculation_policy`, `calculation_value`, `approved_display_value`. Keep the distinct states measured / less-than / reporting-bound / specification-limit / compliance-limit / worst-case-input separate — never collapse into one another. A spec/compliance limit enters a calculation only when the selected method (T1) chooses it; never zeroed merely for being a limit (Diazoxide). `calculation_value` derives from `source_bound`/`source_numeric_value` per the method at calc time, so the same extraction is reproducible under either philosophy without re-OCR.

### T4. EI/RS binary-float → Decimal migration
`docgen_dose` is entirely float (`_f`, `check_column_total`, `selftest_*`), as are `ei_core` (`_parse_conc`, `calculate_ei_tables`, `_ei_mass_basis`), `injection_support` (`_sfloat`, `compute_volume_based`), and `residual_solvent` (`calculate_rs_exposures`, `exposure = amount×ppm/1e6`). Migrate all production calc paths to Decimal/`Quantity`: parsing, unit conversion (`_parse_conc` / `normalize_to_ppm` / `_unit_factor` / `_convert_to_ppm`), quantity multiplication, daily-intake and daily-exposure, PDE/threshold and 30% comparisons, component summation, percentages, drug-product mass (`_ei_mass_basis`, volume×density). Carry exact internal Decimal separately from approved-display rounded values; displayed number must equal computed number with no binary artifact. Keep `DOSE.selftest_structure` / `check_column_total` green under Decimal (retune the 9-dp / 0.001 tolerances to exact where Decimal removes drift; do NOT revert 9-dp rounding — trace contributions ~1e-5 need it).

