## PRIORITY 5 — Infra robustness (must land with T12; parallelism amplifies these)

### T13. 5 MB image limit — downscale, then soft-skip
Claude rejects images >5 MB (400 "image exceeds 5 MB maximum: …bytes"). EI's `annexure_converter` logs and continues; DEG/EG's `deg_eg_annexure_converter.convert_deg_eg_pdf_to_json` (~line 399) raises `ClaudeUnavailableError` and kills the whole annexure. Fix: (1) before base64-encoding each rasterized page, enforce the cap — if the encoded image exceeds ~4.5 MB, re-render at progressively lower DPI (300→200→150→110) and/or JPEG-compress until under 5 MB, then send (CoA pages read fine at ~150 DPI, so most oversized pages SUCCEED after downscale). Apply the SAME size-guard helper in both `annexure_converter` and `deg_eg_annexure_converter`. Extend `make_vision_message` (or a shared helper next to it) so every converter shares one path. (2) If a page still exceeds the cap after downscale, log a warning and SKIP that page, returning what the other pages yielded; never raise for one oversized page. A single-page annexure that fails returns an `error_record` (as EI does) so the mapper treats it as unmatched and generation continues.



