Ground EI/RS composition parsing with the official two-sheet template (JSON schema supplied separately: `formulation_composition_template.json`; sheets **OSD** and **Injectable**; OSD cols Name/Function/`Qty/unit dose`/`Max Daily Dose` per Strength-1/2/3 + Remarks; Injectable adds `Qty/mL`; footnote marks `*`=salt form/state free-base equiv, `@`=removed in processing/traces, `q.s.`=quantity sufficient).

### T15. Grounding as a strong prior, NEVER a hard gate (do not break flexibility)
- **Layer 1 — deterministic fast-path (no LLM):** if a sheet name or header row **fuzzy-matches** OSD/Injectable and columns fuzzy-match the labels, parse directly (sub-second, deterministic) and set `unit_basis` from the sheet type. Fuzzy, not exact-string (accept "OSD (1)", merged headers, shifted rows, stray columns).
